its firmly in Safe Democratic territory.", "watch": "A late outside spending blitz for Hilton or a sustained polling shift after the debate could narrow the margin, though closing a 20-point gap would require an extraordinary change.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Gavin Newsom (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "California's 2026 governor's race is an open-seat contest between Democrat Xavier Becerra and Republican Steve Hilton following Gavin Newsom's two terms. The state's Democratic lean of about twelve points gives Becerra a strong structural advantage, and every major race rating, including Cook Political Report, Inside Elections, Sabato's Crystal Ball and the Silver Bulletin, places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column.\n\nPolling since mid-September shows Becerra ahead by roughly 18 to 25 points among likely voters, and betting markets price his chances near 96 percent. The two campaigns have raised similar amounts, with Hilton holding slightly more cash on hand, but no outside spending wave has emerged on either side. The sole televised debate in early October was testy, with clashes over Trump, taxes and housing, yet produced little evidence the race is tightening. Becerra remains the heavy favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 17.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9936, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9916, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}]}